==Irish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sga|ga}} {{m|sga|fo}}, from {{etyl|cel-pro|ga}} {{m|cel-pro|*uɸo}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ga}} {{m|ine-pro|*upo}}; compare Greek {{m|grc|ὑπό}}, Middle Welsh {{m|wlm|go}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Ulster}} {{IPA|[fˠæː]|lang=ga}}

===Preposition===
{{ga-prep}}

# {{alternative form of|faoi||about, concerning|from=Ulster|lang=ga}}

====Usage notes====
The standard Irish and Connacht form {{m|ga|faoi}} (Munster {{m|ga|fé}}) means both ‘under’ and ‘about, concerning’. In Ulster, these two meanings are split: {{m|ga|faoi}} means ‘under’, while {{lang|ga|''fá''}} means ‘about, concerning’.

